process-record-arrays.m's mover and filler spawned on the machine's GPU
(docs/INPROGRESS.md, Flat records, step 2b): arrays of flat records, alone
and after a fixed part, sent to and from GPU processes, and made, set,
filled and resized there, with none of the host's copies of the messages,
nor the messages, nor the arenas left.
REQUIRES: amdgpu-gpu

RUN: merkc -O2 -fprocess-declarations --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/process-record-arrays.m -o %t2
RUN: %gpu-env timeout -k 1 60 %t2 gpu | FileCheck %S/process-record-arrays.m --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace
RUN: %gpu-env MERK_CHECK_PINNED=1 MERK_CHECK_MESSAGES=1 MERK_CHECK_DEVICE_MEMORY=1 timeout -k 1 60 %t2 gpu 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace

CHECK:0 batches wrong of 40
CHECK-NEXT:Merkurius runtime: 0 chunks of host memory for devices' messages are allocated
CHECK-NEXT:Merkurius runtime: 0 messages are neither read nor freed
CHECK-NEXT:Merkurius runtime: 0 chunks of the devices' arenas and 0 rings are allocated
